    "Data": {
      "Ticketid": "HF-1002",
      "Customername": "Marcus Webb",
      "Subject": "VPN stuck on Connecting from hotel",
      "Body": "I'm traveling this week and GlobalProtect has been sitting on 'Connecting' for ten minutes on the hotel wifi. It worked fine at home on Friday. What should I try?",
      "Category": "Network",
      "Priority": "Medium",
      "Rationale": "KB confirms GlobalProtect setup and specifically says that if the client sits on \u201cConnecting\u201d for more than two minutes, restart the PanGPS service or reboot. It also notes hotel/guest Wi-Fi can block the VPN tunnel and recommends switching to a mobile hotspot. Classified as Network with Medium priority because one user has VPN connectivity degraded while a workaround exists.",
      "Confidence": 0.93,
      "Draftreply": "Hi Marcus,\n\nThanks for letting us know GlobalProtect is stuck on \u201cConnecting\u201d while you\u2019re on the hotel Wi-Fi.\n\nPlease try the following:\n\n1. If GlobalProtect has been on \u201cConnecting\u201d for more than two minutes, restart the PanGPS service from Task Manager.\n2. If that does not clear it, reboot the laptop and try connecting again.\n3. If the hotel or guest Wi-Fi is blocking the VPN tunnel, switch to a mobile hotspot and try the VPN connection from there.\n\nFor reference, the HomeFix VPN status icon turns blue when connected.\n\nBest regards,\nHomeFix Supply Support Team"
    }
  }
